      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article reviews the most common foot deformities and pedal pathomechanical conditions that often result in pain and disability in the elderly. A description of the deformity or condition, its etiology, presenting symptoms, and various nonsurgical approaches to treatment are explored. The primary goal in all cases is to maintain or improve the patient's ability for comfortable, independent ambulation."},
